TTYCHATTER(1)               User Commands               TTYCHATTER(1)

NAME
    ttychatter - OpenRouter terminal chat client, C command-line edition

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter [options] input.txt output.log
    ttychatter --interactive [output.log]
    ttychatter --demo [options] input.txt output.log
    ttychatter --models [--search TEXT] [--model-type TYPE] [--sort KEY]
    ttychatter --select-model
    ttychatter --test-model MODEL
    ttychatter --set-api-key [--gpg]
    ttychatter --forget-api-key
    ttychatter --list
    ttychatter --rename-session OLD NEW
    ttychatter --show-memory SESSION
    ttychatter --edit-memory SESSION
    ttychatter --clear-memory SESSION
    ttychatter --editor-prompt [SESSION]
    ttychatter --search TEXT [--all-sessions]
    ttychatter --config
    ttychatter --set KEY=VALUE
    ttychatter --unset KEY
    ttychatter --doctor
    ttychatter --version
    ttychatter --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter is the traditional Unix command-line C client in the
    ttychatter project.  Unlike the ncurses client, it does not own the full
    terminal screen.  The primary interface is file-in/file-out:

        ttychatter input.txt output.log

    The user creates input.txt using any editor or shell tool.  ttychatter
    sends that input to OpenRouter, appends the AI response to output.log,
    and later uses the same output.log as the session history/context source.

    This edition is intended to be a robust command-line companion to the
    Bash and Python clients.  It keeps feature parity where the feature makes
    sense without ncurses.

USAGE EXAMPLES
    Save an API key in plaintext config:

        ttychatter --set-api-key

    Save an API key encrypted with gpg:

        ttychatter --set-api-key --gpg

    Refresh the model cache:

        ttychatter --update-models

    List cached router models:

        ttychatter --models --model-type routers

    Search cached models:

        ttychatter --models --search llama

    Select a model from a numbered cached list:

        ttychatter --select-model

    Test one model without committing to it:

        ttychatter --test-model openrouter/auto

    Send an input file and append to a session file:

        ttychatter prompt.txt session.log

    Resume a session by using the same output file:

        ttychatter followup.txt session.log

    Attach multiple files:

        ttychatter -a notes.txt -a diagram.png prompt.txt session.log

    Print only the AI response to stdout for shell piping:

        ttychatter --loopback prompt.txt session.log | sed -n '1,20p'

    Start a line-oriented interactive loop:

        ttychatter --interactive session.log

RUNTIME COMMANDS
    In interactive mode, lines beginning with ':' are local ttychatter
    commands.  They are not sent to the AI model.

        :help
        :models
        :routers
        :update-models
        :test-model MODEL
        :model MODEL
        :model-save MODEL
        :favorites
        :favorite MODEL
        :unfavorite MODEL
        :config
        :set KEY VALUE
        :unset KEY
        :set-api-key
        :set-api-key gpg
        :forget-api-key
        :memory
        :clear-memory
        :attach FILE
        :attachments
        :clear-attachments
        :editor
        :search TEXT
        :search-all TEXT
        :credits
        :doctor
        :quit

    To send a literal message beginning with a colon, prefix it with a
    backslash:

        \:this line is sent to the AI

MODEL MANAGEMENT
    ttychatter uses OpenRouter's model catalog.  The model list is cached
    locally so ordinary browsing does not require network access.

        ttychatter --update-models
        ttychatter --models
        ttychatter --models --search TEXT
        ttychatter --models --model-type routers
        ttychatter --models --favorites-only
        ttychatter --models --sort context

    Supported model type filters:

        all
        routers
        fixed
        free
        auto

    Supported sort keys:

        name
        context
        tokens
        type
        favorites

    The C client accepts model filter options similar to the Bash/Python
    clients:

        --min-input-tokens N
        --hide-preview
        --require-tokens
        --all

FAVORITES
    Favorite models are stored as plain text, one model per line.

        ttychatter --favorite-model openrouter/auto
        ttychatter --unfavorite-model openrouter/auto
        ttychatter --favorites

SESSIONS
    Session state is stored in the output log file.  The file remains human
    readable.  Context is reconstructed from recent user/AI blocks in that
    file unless an explicit edited memory snapshot exists.

        ttychatter --list
        ttychatter --rename-session old-name new-name
        ttychatter --show-memory session.log
        ttychatter --edit-memory session.log
        ttychatter --clear-memory session.log

API KEY STORAGE
    ttychatter checks for API keys in this order:

        OPENROUTER_API_KEY environment variable
        TTYCHATTER_API_KEY environment variable
        plaintext config key
        gpg-encrypted key file

    GPG storage uses the external gpg program.  No cryptographic code is
    embedded in ttychatter itself.

CONFIGURATION
    Default config file:

        ~/.config/ttychatter/config

    Important keys include:

        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
        API_KEY_GPG_FILE
        MODEL
        MODEL_CACHE_FILE
        MODEL_FAVORITES_FILE
        MODEL_TYPE_FILTER
        MODEL_SORT_ORDER
        MODEL_FILTER_GENERATE_CONTENT
        MODEL_FILTER_REQUIRE_TOKENS
        MODEL_FILTER_HIDE_PREVIEW
        MODEL_MIN_INPUT_TOKENS
        MODEL_MIN_OUTPUT_TOKENS
        MODEL_TEST_PROMPT
        CONTEXT_TURNS
        SESSION_DIR
        ATTACHMENT_DIR
        CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES
        MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES
        CONFIRM_LIVE_SEND
        STARTUP_NOTICE
        DEMO_MODE
        LOOPBACK
        SEND_INPUT
        THEME
        EDITOR

    Some keys, such as SEND_INPUT and THEME, exist mostly for cross-client
    config parity.  The file-in/file-out C command does not have an input key
    binding or terminal theme in the same sense as the ncurses client.

ATTACHMENTS
    Attach files with -a or --attach.  Text-like files are inserted as text
    parts.  Some media files may be sent as data URLs when model/provider
    support allows it.

    Long fenced code blocks in responses are extracted into ATTACHMENT_DIR.
    Short code blocks remain inline.  The line threshold is controlled by
    CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES.

DEMO MODE
    --demo uses local demo models and local demo responses.  It does not
    require an API key and does not contact OpenRouter.  This is useful for
    testing logs, attachments, loopback, and the interactive command loop.

FILES
    ~/.config/ttychatter/config
        Configuration file.

    ~/.cache/ttychatter/models.json
        Model cache by default.

    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/sessions/
        Default session directory.

    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/attachments/
        Default attachment directory.

VERSION
    ttychatter 0.5.0-c-cli

